==============================================================================
Cross-q synthesis
==============================================================================
smallest Bonferroni floor in this lab: q,k=(12, 7) value=11/36 (0.305556)
smallest bounded p0-cap margin: q,k=(10, 6) value=1/25 (0.040000)
carrier failure ledger:
  p0_AP_not_unique_or_not_max: 8
  scalar_D_inversions: 12139
  scalar_p0_inversions: 12706

Tournament Analysis Hamiltonian path over proof carriers:
  Bonferroni_floor > bounded_nu_minimizer > bounded_p0_cap > AP_difference_profile > scalar_additive_energy

Interpretation:
  The floor and bounded cap mechanisms survive unchanged below q=14.
  Consecutive/AP remains the nu/D extremal row in every bounded bank checked.
  Some non-AP rows have larger p0, but every bounded-bank p0 stays below cap.
  Scalar additive energy is already non-monotone in easier q, so it is
  diagnostic only; the durable additive object is AP-facing difference
  profile majorization plus labelled residual control.
